{"Title":"An Act to provide identification to youth and adults experiencing homelessness","BillNumber":"H3360","DocketNumber":"HD2780","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"K_K1","Name":"Kay Khan","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/K_K1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T16:17:48.417"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"K_K1","Name":"Kay Khan","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/K_K1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T16:17:48.4166667"},{"Id":"JCD1","Name":"James C. Arena-DeRosa","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JCD1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-08T10:06:43.21"},{"Id":"SBA1","Name":"Shirley B. Arriaga","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SBA1","ResponseDate":"2023-05-09T13:32:56.2333333"},{"Id":"BMA1","Name":"Brian M. Ashe","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BMA1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-09T19:41:55.14"},{"Id":"DFC1","Name":"Daniel Cahill","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/DFC1","ResponseDate":"2024-01-08T12:57:21.4333333"},{"Id":"PLC1","Name":"Peter Capano","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PLC1","ResponseDate":"2024-01-05T11:57:33.4833333"},{"Id":"M_C1","Name":"Mike Connolly","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/M_C1","ResponseDate":"2023-09-06T12:31:56.5866667"},{"Id":"CAD1","Name":"Carol A. Doherty","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CAD1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-20T21:42:00.96"},{"Id":"K_D1","Name":"Kate Donaghue","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/K_D1","ResponseDate":"2023-12-06T11:58:25.63"},{"Id":"PAD1","Name":"Patricia A. Duffy","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PAD1","ResponseDate":"2023-05-09T10:45:27.15"},{"Id":"JBE0","Name":"James B. Eldridge","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JBE0","ResponseDate":"2023-03-04T08:43:35.4666667"},{"Id":"CMG1","Name":"Colleen M. Garry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CMG1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-08T12:03:05.96"},{"Id":"CLG1","Name":"Carmine Lawrence Gentile","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CLG1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-08T11:56:32.3933333"},{"Id":"N_H1","Name":"Natalie M. Higgins","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/N_H1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-23T10:57:24.3"},{"Id":"REH1","Name":"Russell E. Holmes","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/REH1","ResponseDate":"2023-06-07T16:08:13.5766667"},{"Id":"V_H1","Name":"Vanna Howard","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/V_H1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-31T12:52:45.1333333"},{"Id":"MPK1","Name":"Michael P. Kushmerek","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MPK1","ResponseDate":"2023-03-24T12:24:11.2466667"},{"Id":"JBL0","Name":"Joan B. Lovely","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JBL0","ResponseDate":"2023-04-12T14:35:01.9733333"},{"Id":"S_M1","Name":"Samantha Montaño","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/S_M1","ResponseDate":"2023-05-04T13:13:15.14"},{"Id":"TTN1","Name":"Tram T. Nguyen","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/TTN1","ResponseDate":"2023-12-19T14:35:28.9066667"},{"Id":"RLR0","Name":"Rebecca L. Rausch","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RLR0","ResponseDate":"2023-03-02T15:30:44.9433333"},{"Id":"DMR1","Name":"David M. Rogers","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/DMR1","ResponseDate":"2023-10-24T10:44:39.8966667"},{"Id":"JFM1","Name":"John Francis Moran","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JFM1","ResponseDate":"2023-09-25T15:40:15.8233333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H3360/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Khan of Newton, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 3360) of Kay Khan and others that the Registrar of Motor Vehicles provide identification to youth and adults experiencing homelessness.  Transportation.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 8E of Chapter 90 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by adding the following 2 paragraphs:- \r\n\tWhen establishing criteria for identification cards, the registrar’s regulations shall include a process for a person who is homeless or is an unaccompanied homeless youth to apply for a Massachusetts identification card and to waive any fees associated with obtaining the identification card; provided, however, that the process shall allow for a person who is homeless or is an unaccompanied homeless youth to submit proof of residency by providing documentation that is satisfactory to the registrar and that: (i) is from an entity that provides services in the commonwealth, including, but not limited to, homeless service providers; or (ii) is evidence of services that the person received from a department, division, office or agency of the executive office of health and  human services. The registrar and the state secretary shall enter into a memorandum of understanding under section 42G ½ of chapter 51 to implement this paragraph, as appropriate.\r\n\tFor the purposes of this section, the following terms shall have the following meanings:\r\n\t“Homeless”, shall have the same meaning as in section 103 of the Stewart B. McKinney Homeless Assistance Act of 1987, 42 USC 11302(a), as amended. \r\n\t“Unaccompanied homeless youth”, a person who: (i) is 24 years of age or younger; (ii) is not in the physical custody or care of a parent or legal guardian; and (iii) lacks a fixed, regular and adequate nighttime residence.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J27","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J27"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}